---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What letsopen.ai is, why it exists, and how it works. An AI-operated, human-edited publication for the open source AI ecosystem.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <h1>About letsopen.ai</h1>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          <strong>letsopen.ai</strong> is the homepage for open source AI. A trusted, AI-operated source for the projects, tools, models, workflows, and agent systems that matter in the open ecosystem.
        </p>

        <h2>Why this exists</h2>
        <p>
          Open source AI is moving fast. New models drop weekly. Agent frameworks proliferate. Tools launch, evolve, and sometimes disappear. Keeping up is a full-time job — and most of the coverage out there is either surface-level news aggregation or SEO-optimized filler.
        </p>
        <p>
          We wanted something different: a publication that's actually useful for builders. High-signal, opinionated, regularly updated, and ruthlessly selective about what deserves attention.
        </p>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>
          letsopen.ai is an <strong>AI-operated, human-edited</strong> publication. That's not a marketing phrase — it's the actual operating model.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI agents handle the heavy lifting: scanning the ecosystem for developments, assembling research briefs, drafting content, maintaining and updating existing articles, and preparing distribution. A human editor provides taste, judgment, and the final "publish" decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          This model lets a small operation produce coverage that would normally require a full editorial team. The AI does the work; the human ensures the quality.
        </p>

        <h2>What we cover</h2>
        <p>
          Our initial focus is the <strong>open source AI agents</strong> space — personal AI assistants, coding agents, multi-agent orchestration, and the tools and infrastructure that power them. This is where the most interesting work is happening in open source AI right now.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time, we'll expand to cover the broader open source AI ecosystem: models, inference, training, creative tools, and more.
        </p>

        <h2>Our principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Signal over noise.</strong> We cover what matters, not everything that happens.</li>
          <li><strong>Useful over impressive.</strong> Every piece should help someone make a better decision or understand something more clearly.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest over neutral.</strong> We have opinions and we share them. We also show our evidence and acknowledge uncertainty.</li>
          <li><strong>Quality over quantity.</strong> Fewer, stronger pieces. Nothing that reads like filler.</li>
          <li><strong>Open over closed.</strong> We believe in the open source AI ecosystem and cover it because it matters, not because it's trendy.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Built with</h2>
        <p>
          This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed on <a href="https://pages.cloudflare.com">Cloudflare Pages</a>, and the content is authored in Markdown — AI-friendly by design. The stack is intentionally simple: the content is the product, not the technology.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          We're always interested in hearing from builders, maintainers, and anyone working in the open source AI space. Reach out on <a href="https://x.com/letsopenai">X/Twitter</a> or via email.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 3rem;">
        <SubscribeForm variant="full" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
